="epo"><addressbook><name>NIPPON ELECTRIC CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI KENICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARA, YOUICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CHEN, SHUGUANG</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NEC CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, KENICHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARA YOUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>CHEN SHUGUANG</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI KENICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARA, YOUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CHEN, SHUGUANG</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, KENICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A micromachine which can be mass-produced, is cheap, and has high performance. The machine comprises a support member (7) provided near a gap of a signal line on a base (1) and has a predetermined height from the surface of the base (1), a flexible beam member (cantilevered arm (8)) which projects from the support member (7) generally parallel to the surface of the base (1) and part of which faces to the gap, a contact electrode (5) provided on the base side of the beam member and facing to at least the gap, and a lower electrode (4) provided on the base (1) and facing to part of the beam member. The beam member is conductive from the portion connected to the support member (7) to the portion facing to the lower electrode (4) and consequently functions as an upper electrode (9). The thermal expansion coefficient is generally symmetric in the direction of the thickness perpendicular to the surface of the base (1) at least in the region from the portion connected to the support member (7) to the portion facing to the lower electrode (4).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Il est possible de produire en masse et économiquement une micromachine à hautes performances qui comprend: un support (7) situé près d'une discontinuité du conducteur de signaux sur une base (1) dont il saille de la surface d'une hauteur donnée; un bras (8) souple en porte à faux partant du support (7), sensiblement parallèle à la surface de la base (1) et dont une partie fait face à la discontinuité; une électrode de contact (5) située à la base du bras et faisant face à au moins la discontinuité; et une électrode inférieure (4) disposée sur la base (1) face à une partie du bras. Ledit bras, conducteur entre la partie reliée au support (7) et la partie faisant face à l'électrode inférieure, (4) sert donc d'électrode supérieure (9). Le coefficient de dilatation thermique est sensiblement symétrique dans le sens de l'épaisseur normalement à la surface de la base (1), au moins dans la zone comprise entre la partie reliée au support (7) et la partie faisant face à l'électrode inférieure (4)</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>